The categories of information excluded from the definition of Confidential Information include:

(a) Information that is or becomes publicly available through no fault of the receiving Party;
(b) Information that was already known to the receiving Party prior to disclosure, as shown by written records;
(c) Information that is independently developed by the receiving Party without use of the disclosing Party's Confidential Information; or
(d) Information that is rightfully obtained from a third party without restriction [Source 1].

